From: Ely Office
Subject: LOK: Impress lists, adds, duplicates, deletes and moves slides by index

- .uno:ElySlides lists every slide: name, AutoLayout id, the title box's
  text ("" when empty) and whether it is hidden.
- .uno:ElySlide (Verb, Slide, Value) works on slides by index, in one
  undo step: add puts a new slide with layout Value at index Slide,
  duplicate copies Slide after it, delete removes Slide (never the only
  one), move makes Slide index Value.
- The view keeps showing the same slide; deleting it shows a neighbour,
  as Impress does. Slide marks are kept across a move.
- The slide sorter follows the main view's slide across page changes:
  after a model change it takes the main view's slide, not the old
  index (its delayed switch would show whatever slide moved there), and
  when an undo removes slides it keeps that slide instead of falling
  back to, and showing, the first slide.
- A bad index, verb or layout changes nothing.

